        "original_id": "383f3498-9f94-5271-bb11-dae86bc723f6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ward Bond, John Wayne, Patricia Neal, Philip Carey, George Waggner\n- Works: Operation Pacific, Wagon Train\n- Topics: American film and television\n\nFacts:\n- Ward Bond was the stage name of Wardell Edwin Bond, who was born on April 9, 1903, and died on November 5, 1960.\n- Operation Pacific is a 1951 World War II submarine film directed by George Waggner.\n- Operation Pacific stars John Wayne and Patricia Neal and features Ward Bond and Philip Carey.\n- Ward Bond was an American film character actor known for his rugged appearance and easygoing charm.\n- Ward Bond appeared in more than two hundred films.\n- Ward Bond appeared in the NBC television series Wagon Train from 1957 to 1960.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
